oners that do not deploy as intended may increase the risk of injury.","remedy":"Toyota will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the ECU and install a noise filter between the air bag control module and its wire harness, as necessary, free of charge.  Owners were notified of the safety risk beginning March 2, 2020.  A second letter notifying owners of the remedy repair will be mailed between March 16, 2020 and June 27, 2020.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-888-270-9371.  Toyota's numbers for this recall are 20TB03, 20TA03 and 20TA05.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2891976,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20V024000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":25,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2012","make":"TOYOTA","model":"MATRIX"},{"year":"2011","make":"TOYOTA","model":"MATRIX"},{"year":"2013","make":"TOYOTA","model":"MATRIX"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON HYBRID"},{"year":"2013","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON HYBRID"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON HYBRID"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON HYBRID"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON HYBRID"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON HYBRID"},{"year":"2013","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2011","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2012","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2012","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"19V503000","received":"2019-06-28","manufacturer":"Southeast Toyota Distributors, LLC","component":"EQUIPMENT:OTHER:LABELS","summary":"Southeast Toyota Distributors, LLC (SET) is recalling certain 2017-2019 Toyota Camry, Corolla, Rav4, Sienna, and Yaris iA vehicles equipped with factory-installed floor mats.  The load carrying capacity modification label may be incorrect.  As such, these vehicles fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard (FMVSS) number 110, \"Tire Selection and Rims.\"","consequence":"An incorrect label may lead to unintentionally overloading the vehicle, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"SET will notify owners and provide a corrected label for placement over the inaccurate label, free of charge.  The recall began August 23, 2019.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-888-270-9371.  SET's number for this recall is SET19A.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1325,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V503000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":15,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"SIENNA"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"YARIS"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"YARIS"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"SIENNA"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"YARIS"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"SIENNA"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"17V295000","received":"2017-05-02","manufacturer":"Gulf States Toyota, Inc.","component":"TIRES:TEMPORARY/EMERGENCY SPARE TIRE","summary":"Gulf States Toyota, Inc. (Gulf States) is recalling certain 2017 4Runner , 86, Avalon, Camry, Camry Hybrid, Corolla, Corolla iM, Highlander, Highlander Hybrid, Prius, Prius C, RAV4, RAV4 Hybrid, Sienna  and Yaris vehicles.  The spare tire air pressure was not adjusted to the proper pressure as stated on the Tire Pressure Label.","consequence":"A spare tire that is not inflated to the proper value may not perform as intended, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Gulf States will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the spare tires, adjusting their pressure as necessary, free of charge.  The recall began June 15, 2017.  Owners may contact Gulf States customer service at 1-800-444-1074.  Toyota's number for this recall is 17R2.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":409,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=17V295000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":15,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"PRIUS"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"SIENNA"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"PRIUS C"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"86"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER HYBRID"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY HYBRID"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA IM"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4 HV"},{"yea